��i<?php exit; ?>a:2:{s:7:"content";O:8:"stdClass":24:{s:2:"ID";i:5352;s:11:"post_author";s:1:"1";s:9:"post_date";s:19:"2026-04-01 09:57:01";s:13:"post_date_gmt";s:19:"2026-04-01 09:57:01";s:12:"post_content";s:1403:"<p>Contributions need a bar: visual regression tests, keyboard paths, and documentation that a contractor can follow on day two.</p><p>Design systems collapse when they are a Figma shrine nobody ships. Tokens in code, accessible components, and versioning separate toys from products.</p><h2 class="blog-details__h2">What we are seeing in practice</h2><h3 class="blog-details__h3">Metrics that actually matter here</h3><p>NSC treats the system as a product with its own roadmap, not a side project for one designer.</p><ul class="blog-details__list"><li>Name a design-dev partnership owner</li><li>Deprecate components on a schedule</li><li>Measure adoption, not only downloads</li></ul><figure class="blog-details__figure wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://nsc.test/wp-content/themes/NSC-Software/frontend/build/img/blog6.webp" alt="Design Systems That Scale Across Products — delivery context" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="675" /></figure><figure class="blog-details__figure wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://nsc.test/wp-content/themes/NSC-Software/frontend/build/img/blog3.webp" alt="Design Systems That Scale Across Products — team collaboration" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="675" /></figure><ol class="blog-details__list"><li>Name a design-dev partnership owner</li><li>Deprecate components on a schedule</li><li>Measure adoption, not only downloads</li></ol>";s:10:"post_title";s:41:"Design Systems That Scale Across Products";s:12:"post_excerpt";s:290:"Design Systems That Scale Across Products — Design systems collapse when they are a Figma shrine nobody ships. Tokens in code, accessible components, and versioning separate toys from products. Contributions need a bar: visual regression tests, keyboard paths, and documentation that a…"